course: dictionary
lesson: 11241
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues around the word show you which meaning the writer wants. «Most children worked on farms or in workshops, and most people learned a trade by watching and doing, like Patrick's plumber uncle.» Here the workshop is a place, because people learn a trade there by doing the work.
explain: Ask what happens in the workshop. In a writing workshop, people meet to learn by doing something together, such as writing their own stories. «Ella spent Saturday at a writing workshop.» The word writing and the idea of doing it together tell you the workshop is a class, not a room.
explain: Check the sentence with your meaning. «Many people in Rome were enslaved and worked in houses, fields, mines and workshops.» Workshops are one of the places where people worked, so the list tells you it means a place where things are made. If your meaning fits every part of the sentence, you have probably chosen the right one.
fact: A workshop is a room or building where people make or fix things, often with tools.
fact: A workshop can also be a meeting or class where people learn by doing something together.
fact: «In the workshop» usually means in the place where things are made or fixed.
fact: «A workshop on» a topic means a class about that topic, such as «a workshop on science».
fact: Santa's workshop is a famous place from stories, where toys are made.
exercise: «Most children worked on farms or in workshops.» Find and copy the word that names a place where people worked. | Spartacus | revolt | freed | *workshops
exercise: «Ella spent Saturday at a writing workshop, where everyone read their stories aloud.» What does workshop mean here? | A room full of tools for fixing bikes | *A class where people learn by doing something together | A shop that sells books | A holiday camp for children
exercise: Grandad says he is going to his workshop in the shed to fix the chair. What does workshop mean? | *A place where things are made or fixed | A school lesson on wood | A kind of shed roof | A meeting about garden plants
test: In «a bike repair workshop», what happens there? | People sing songs together | *Bikes are fixed | Bikes are sold to customers | Children are taught to ride
test: What does «a workshop on science» mean? | A science museum with glass cases | *A class where people learn science by doing experiments | A science book for sale | A test with no answers
exam: «Patrick's uncle learned his trade in workshops, by watching and doing.» Here workshops means | school subjects | meetings about trade laws | a type of food | *places where people make or fix things
